  "limitations": [
    "The kernel test is not an end-to-end retrieval benchmark.",
    "LongMemEval was evaluated as raw-session reranking with a BM25 lexical proxy; this does not evaluate frozen production summaries, Qwen embeddings, answer generation, or MSC.",
    "The corrected Pareto macro Recall@5 point estimate is 0.003 below the fixed weighted-sum baseline; the paired outcomes are 1 Pareto win, 496 ties, and 3 weighted-sum wins. Shared candidate sessions connect all questions into one component, so no question-level significance or generalization claim is justified.",
    "Thirteen questions contain repeated non-qrel candidate session IDs with identical content and distinct dates; candidate positions are retained separately as specified, and this source-data irregularity may influence position-wise ranking.",
    "Seventy-five of 948 qrel labels are future-dated relative to their question dates; the full-candidate analysis preserves the supplied haystack, while strict-cutoff sensitivity counts unavailable qrels as misses.",
    "Latency is a warmed JUnit microbenchmark on one machine, not production p50/p95 latency.",
    "LongTermMemoryEnhancedTest's trade-off fixture has two candidates with topK=2 and asserts membership only; it does not exercise adapter truncation, assert returned order, or demonstrate graph-activation effects. Generic ranker tests cover truncation separately.",
    "The successful targeted test log reports test compilation as up to date and does not retain the invoked Maven command. A later diagnostic test-source compilation failed on 17 unrelated Phase151/Phase152 benchmark-test errors before Surefire; therefore the archived pass is not a fresh compile-and-test proof for the current source snapshot.",
    "JaCoCo reports 100% instruction, branch, line, and method coverage for the ParetoMemoryRanker class; overall project coverage is not established.",
    "The current long-term-memory vector query does not apply userId as a filter; tenant isolation requires separate remediation and verification before production-safety claims."
  ],
